[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've put three filter layouts side by side in a browser tab, using real rows from the sample data. If it didn't open
  on its own, here's the link:

  [94m]8;id=1av9n41;http://localhost:50524/?key=1ae8e6f764367aeaf8f3a7f78197c54d748bd7b147c38def2e43e0a81b72a3f0\http://localhost:50524/?key=1ae8e6f764367aeaf8f3a7f78197c54d748bd7b147c38def2e43e0a81b72a3f0[39m]8;;\

  This tab uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.

  - [1mA. Three views + week select.[0m A "Show" radio group (All events / Failed sign-ins / Security changes) and one "Week"
    select listing the roughly 13 calendar weeks in the 90-day window, plus "All 90 days". Two controls, one click each.
  - [1mB. Type checkboxes + date range.[0m All nine types as checkboxes in your three groups, plus From/To date pickers and a
    presets select. This is the most flexible, but it's the heaviest: it needs date validation and makes the biggest
    diff.
  - [1mC. Three views + "Week starting" date.[0m The same radio group as A, but you pick any start day and the table shows
    that day and the six after it.

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It maps one-to-one onto the three things you said people want. It uses only components the guidelines
  already define: a RadioGroup, which allows a horizontal layout for three short labels, and a Select, which is meant
  for six or more options. It has no invalid states, so there are no validation messages. The trade-off: you can only
  pick calendar weeks. If someone wants Wednesday through Tuesday, they'd look at two weeks.

  Click one in the browser if you like, but please answer here in the terminal.

  The mockups are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo, and that folder isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m. I haven't changed
  [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m because it's outside today's task. I'll just keep those files out of any commit.

